# Project Context

This project studies motor-imagery (MI) EEG decoding on the Shanghai University
WBCIC-SHU MI-EEG dataset (2019 World Robot Conference BCI contest data).
The long-term goal is a *confidence-aware, online-adaptive, multi-subagent*
pretraining framework for cross-subject MI decoding. See `docs/PROJECT_BRIEF.md`
and `docs/references/ChatGPT-EEG-MI-pretraining.md` (the senior's chat record,
which is the source of the project's core idea).

## Core dataset (verified on this server)

- Focus on the **2C dataset** (two-class) first.
- Dataset root (READ-ONLY): `/share/workspace2/moto_imagination/WBCIC_SHU`.
- Raw BDF per session: `sourcedata/2C dataset/sub-XXX/ses-YY/eeg/{data.bdf, evt.bdf}`.
- Paper-processed `.mat` per session: `derivatives/2C dataset_processeddata/sub-XXX/ses-YY/eeg/sub-XXX_ses-YY_task-motorimagery_eeg.mat`.
- **51** subject folders exist on disk (note: `participants_2C.tsv` lists 52 ids,
  the README mentions 53 two-class participants). **Always enumerate subjects from
  disk; never hardcode the count.**
- **3 sessions** per subject.
- **2 classes**: left-hand grasping MI (event value 1) vs right-hand grasping MI
  (event value 2). Map to internal labels {1->0, 2->1}.
- **200 trials per session**, 100 per class.
- Raw sampling rate **1000 Hz**; preprocessing target **250 Hz**.
- Raw channel layout (VERIFIED via `scripts/check_raw_bdf.py` on sub-001/ses-01):
  **64 channels = 59 EEG + 1 ECG + 4 EOG**. EEG names (Fpz ... O2) are in
  `task-motorimagery_channels.tsv`; ECG is `ECG`; EOG are `HEOR, HEOL, VEOU, VEOL`.
  NOTE: `task-motorimagery_eeg.json` says "1 EOG, 4 ECG" — that count is **swapped**
  vs the actual channel names; trust the names. Some aux channels can be flat
  (ECG and VEOL were flat in the first 10 s on sub-001/ses-01) — verify validity.
- Target processed tensor per session: `[trials, channels, time] = [200, 58, 1000]`
  (58 = 59 EEG minus Pz after Pz re-referencing; 1000 = 4 s @ 250 Hz).
- The paper `.mat` stores `data` as `[channels, time, trials] = [58, 1000, 200]`
  and `labels` as `[1, 200]` with values {1, 2}. Our convention transposes to
  `[trials, channels, time]`.

## Main research pipeline

1. Load raw BDF data with Python + MNE.
2. Preprocess raw EEG, optionally using ECG/EOG channels for artifact cleaning.
3. Save processed trials as `.npy`/`.npz` in `[trials, channels, time]`.
4. Reproduce baseline models: EEGNet, DeepConvNet, FBCNet.
5. Run repeated 41/10 subject-wise cross-subject pretraining.
6. Fine-tune on target-subject Session 1.
7. Online test-then-update adaptation on target Session 2 and Session 3.

## Hard invariants (never violate)

- Do NOT modify, write to, or delete anything outside `/share/home/yuan/SYX`.
  The dataset directory is strictly read-only.
- Saved processed data is always `[trials, channels, time]`.
- Split by **subject**, never by trial, for cross-subject experiments.
- Target subjects must never leak into source-subject training.
- Online learning is **test-then-update**: predict first, record metrics, then update.
- Development happens in the conda env `mi_torch`.
- Never launch training on the Slurm login node (see `40-server-slurm`).
